/-!
# The affine normalization comparison after a field extension is a universal homeomorphism

Let `k` be a field, `R` a normal `k`-algebra and `K/k` an extension of fields. Write
`T = R ⊗[k] K`, let `S = T / nilradical T` be its reduction and let `S'` be the integral closure
of `S` in its total ring of fractions, so that `Spec S' ⟶ Spec T` is the affine model of the
normalization of the base change `Spec R ×_{Spec k} Spec K`. The main result is that this
morphism is a universal homeomorphism, for an arbitrary extension `K/k`.

This is the affine content of the "universal homeomorphism" assertion of Tag 0C3N, where the
base scheme is `Spec R` with `R` normal; the general case is assembled from it over an affine
open cover of a normal model.

The argument is the source's. Factor `K/k` as a separable extension `F/k` followed by a purely
inseparable extension `K/F`. Over `F` the ring `A = F ⊗[k] R` is still normal, because a
separable extension is geometrically normal (Tag 0C30) and a geometrically normal algebra stays
normal after tensoring with a normal one (Tag 06DF); in particular `A` is reduced and integrally
closed in its total ring of fractions (Tag 034M). Pure inseparability of `K/F` makes every
element of `T = A ⊗[F] K` acquire a `p`-power lying in the image of `A`, where `p` is the
exponential characteristic. That single condition propagates through the reduction and the
integral closure, and a ring map all of whose target elements have a `p`-power in its image and
whose kernel is nilpotent induces a universal homeomorphism on spectra: integrality is immediate,
universal injectivity comes from injectivity of the iterated Frobenius on the receiving field, and
surjectivity from Mathlib's homeomorphism criterion for such a map.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.universalHomeomorphism_specMap_of_pow_mem_range`: a ring map with nilpotent
  kernel such that every element of the target has a `p`-th power iterate in its image induces a
  universal homeomorphism of spectra, `p` the exponential characteristic of a base field.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.universalHomeomorphism_normalization_of_pow_mem_range`: the same hypothesis
  on a map out of an integrally closed reduced ring passes to the normalization of the reduction
  of the target.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_separable_purelyInseparable_factorization`: every extension of fields
  factors as a separable extension followed by a purely inseparable one.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.universalHomeomorphism_normalization_tensorProduct_of_normal`: the
  normalization of the reduction of `R ⊗[k] K` is a universal homeomorphism over `R ⊗[k] K`, for
  `R` a normal `k`-algebra and `K/k` arbitrary.

## Implementation notes

The exponential characteristic is carried as an `ExpChar k p` instance on the base field rather
than as a hypothesis on the rings, so that it is available in characteristic zero with `p = 1`,
where the `p`-power condition degenerates to surjectivity up to nilpotents and the argument
still applies verbatim.

The separable–purely inseparable factorization is built as the separable closure of `K` over the
subfield generated by a transcendence basis. That the resulting `F/k` is separable, rather than
merely separably generated, is `isSeparableExtension_of_isSeparablyGenerated`, which transports
a transcendence basis witnessing separable generation across an arbitrary base change.

The target of the comparison is spelled as the composite
`T ⟶ T / nilradical T ⟶ integralClosure (T / nilradical T) (FractionRing (T / nilradical T))`
rather than through any scheme-level normalization construction, so that the statement is
independent of how the normalization of a scheme is assembled.

No Tag 0C3N attribute is attached in this file. The tag's "universal homeomorphism" assertion is
about the comparison for an arbitrary scheme locally of finite type over `k`; the results here
cover the affine case over a normal base, which carries a normality hypothesis the assertion does
not have, so these results do not cover the label and the tag is not attached. Assembling the general case from these results additionally needs the universal property
of the normalization of a scheme, birationality of the normalization morphism, and finiteness of
the normalization of a scheme of finite type over a field, none of which is available.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0C3N](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C3N)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 04DF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04DF)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0C30](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C30)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 06DF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/06DF)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory

open scoped nonZeroDivisors

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- If every element of `S` has a `p ^ n`-th power in the image of `f`, for `p` an exponential
characteristic, then every element of `S` has a positive power in the image of `f`. -/
private theorem exists_pos_pow_mem_range_of_expChar {k R S : Type*} [Field k] [CommRing R]
    [CommRing S] (f : R →+* S) (p : ℕ) [ExpChar k p]
    (hpow : ∀ s : S, ∃ n : ℕ, s ^ p ^ n ∈ f.range) : ∀ s : S, ∃ n > 0, s ^ n ∈ f.range :=
  fun s => let ⟨n, hn⟩ := hpow s; ⟨p ^ n, expChar_pow_pos k p n, hn⟩

/-- A ring map such that every element of the target has a positive power in the image is
integral. -/
private theorem isIntegral_of_pos_pow_mem_range {R S : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S]
    [Algebra R S] (hpow : ∀ s : S, ∃ n > 0, s ^ n ∈ (algebraMap R S).range) :
    Algebra.IsIntegral R S :=
  ⟨fun s => by
    obtain ⟨n, hn, r, hr⟩ := hpow s
    exact IsIntegral.of_pow hn (hr ▸ isIntegral_algebraMap)⟩

/-- Let `k` be a field of exponential characteristic `p` and `f : R →+* S` a ring map out of a
`k`-algebra whose kernel consists of nilpotent elements. If every element of `S` has a `p ^ n`-th
power in the image of `f`, then `Spec S ⟶ Spec R` is a universal homeomorphism. -/
public theorem universalHomeomorphism_specMap_of_pow_mem_range
    {k R S : Type u} [Field k] [CommRing R] [CommRing S] [Algebra k R]
    (f : R →+* S) (p : ℕ) [ExpChar k p]
    (hker : RingHom.ker f ≤ nilradical R)
    (hpow : ∀ s : S, ∃ n : ℕ, s ^ p ^ n ∈ f.range) :
    UniversalHomeomorphism (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom f)) := by
  apply (universalHomeomorphism_iff_integral_universallyInjective_surjective _).2
  have hpos := exists_pos_pow_mem_range_of_expChar (k := k) f p hpow
  have hint : f.IsIntegral :=
    let : Algebra R S := f.toAlgebra
    fun s => (isIntegral_of_pos_pow_mem_range (R := R) hpos).isIntegral s
  refine ⟨IsIntegralHom.SpecMap_iff.mpr hint, ?_, ?_⟩
  · apply ((tfae_universallyInjective _).out 2 1).mp
    intro F _ a b hab
    obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ := Spec.map_surjective a
    obtain ⟨b, rfl⟩ := Spec.map_surjective b
    have hab' : a.hom.comp f = b.hom.comp f :=
      congrArg CommRingCat.Hom.hom (Spec.map_injective (by simpa only [← Spec.map_comp] using hab))
    apply congrArg Spec.map
    apply CommRingCat.hom_ext
    ext s
    have : ExpChar F p :=
      expChar_of_injective_ringHom ((a.hom.comp f).comp (algebraMap k R)).injective p
    obtain ⟨n, r, hr⟩ := hpow s
    apply iterateFrobenius_inj F p n
    show a.hom s ^ p ^ n = b.hom s ^ p ^ n
    rw [← map_pow, ← map_pow, ← hr]
    exact congrArg (fun g : R →+* F => g r) hab'
  · exact ⟨(PrimeSpectrum.isHomeomorph_comap f hpos hker).surjective⟩

/-- Let `f : R →+* S` be injective, sending non-zero-divisors to non-zero-divisors, such that
every element of `S` has a `p ^ n`-th power in the image of `f`. Then every element of the total
ring of fractions of `S` has a `p ^ n`-th power in the image of the induced map
`FractionRing R →+* FractionRing S`. -/
public theorem exists_pow_mem_range_fractionRing
    {R S : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S]
    (f : R →+* S) (hf : Function.Injective f)
    (hreg : R⁰ ≤ (S⁰).comap f) (p : ℕ)
    (hpow : ∀ s : S, ∃ n : ℕ, s ^ p ^ n ∈ f.range)
    (x : FractionRing S) :
    ∃ n : ℕ, x ^ p ^ n ∈
      (IsLocalization.map (FractionRing S) f hreg :
        FractionRing R →+* FractionRing S).range := by
  obtain ⟨a, b, rfl⟩ := IsLocalization.exists_mk'_eq S⁰ x
  obtain ⟨n, r, hr⟩ := hpow a
  obtain ⟨m, s, hs⟩ := hpow b.1
  have hsreg : s ∈ R⁰ := mem_nonZeroDivisors_of_injective hf (hs ▸ pow_mem b.2 _)
  refine ⟨n + m, IsLocalization.mk' (FractionRing R) (r ^ p ^ m)
    (⟨s, hsreg⟩ ^ p ^ n), ?_⟩
  rw [IsLocalization.map_mk', ← IsLocalization.mk'_pow]
  congr 1
  · simp only [map_pow, hr, ← pow_mul, ← pow_add]
  · apply Subtype.ext
    show f (s ^ p ^ n) = (b : S) ^ p ^ (n + m)
    simp only [map_pow, hs, ← pow_mul, ← pow_add, Nat.add_comm]

/-- Let `R → S` be an injective integral ring map with `R` integrally closed, sending
non-zero-divisors to non-zero-divisors, such that every element of `S` has a `p ^ n`-th power in
the image of `R`. Then every element of the integral closure of `S` in its total ring of
fractions has a `p ^ n`-th power in the image of `S`. -/
public theorem exists_pow_mem_range_normalization_of_isIntegrallyClosed
    {R S : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S] [Algebra R S]
    [IsIntegrallyClosed R] [Algebra.IsIntegral R S]
    (hf : Function.Injective (algebraMap R S))
    (hreg : R⁰ ≤ (S⁰).comap (algebraMap R S)) (p : ℕ)
    (hpow : ∀ s : S, ∃ n : ℕ, s ^ p ^ n ∈ (algebraMap R S).range)
    (b : integralClosure S (FractionRing S)) :
    ∃ n : ℕ, b ^ p ^ n ∈ (algebraMap S (integralClosure S (FractionRing S))).range := by
  let φ : FractionRing R →ₐ[R] FractionRing S :=
    { toRingHom := IsLocalization.map (FractionRing S) (algebraMap R S) hreg
      commutes' := fun r => IsLocalization.map_eq hreg r }
  have hφ : Function.Injective φ := by
    refine (IsLocalization.injective_iff_map_algebraMap_eq R⁰ φ.toRingHom).mpr fun a a' =>
      ⟨congrArg φ.toRingHom, fun h => congrArg (algebraMap R (FractionRing R)) (hf ?_)⟩
    apply IsFractionRing.injective S (FractionRing S)
    simpa only [φ, AlgHom.coe_mk, IsLocalization.map_eq] using h
  obtain ⟨n, c, hc⟩ := exists_pow_mem_range_fractionRing (algebraMap R S) hf hreg p hpow b.1
  have hcint : _root_.IsIntegral R c := (isIntegral_algHom_iff φ hφ).mp (by
    show _root_.IsIntegral R ((IsLocalization.map (FractionRing S) (algebraMap R S) hreg) c)
    rw [hc]
    exact (isIntegral_trans b.1 b.2).pow _)
  obtain ⟨r, hr⟩ := IsIntegrallyClosed.algebraMap_eq_of_integral hcint
  refine ⟨n, algebraMap R S r, ?_⟩
  apply Subtype.ext
  show algebraMap S (FractionRing S) (algebraMap R S r) = (b : FractionRing S) ^ p ^ n
  rw [← hc, ← hr, IsLocalization.map_eq]

/-- An injective ring map `f : R →+* S` into a reduced ring, such that every element of `S` has
a positive power in the image of `f`, sends non-zero-divisors of `R` to non-zero-divisors of
`S`. -/
public theorem nonZeroDivisors_le_comap_of_pow_mem_range
    {R S : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S] [_root_.IsReduced S]
    (f : R →+* S) (hf : Function.Injective f)
    (hpow : ∀ s : S, ∃ n > 0, s ^ n ∈ f.range) : R⁰ ≤ (S⁰).comap f := by
  intro a ha
  apply mem_nonZeroDivisors_iff_left.mpr
  intro x hax
  obtain ⟨n, hn, r, hr⟩ := hpow x
  have he : a ^ n * r = 0 := hf (by
    simp only [map_mul, map_pow, hr, map_zero, ← mul_pow, hax, zero_pow hn.ne'])
  have hr0 : r = 0 := mem_nonZeroDivisors_iff_left.mp (pow_mem ha n) r he
  exact isNilpotent_iff_eq_zero.mp ⟨n, by rw [← hr, hr0, map_zero]⟩

/-- An injective ring map out of a reduced ring stays injective after composing with the
quotient of its target by the nilradical. -/
public theorem injective_quotient_nilradical_comp
    {R S : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S] [_root_.IsReduced R]
    (f : R →+* S) (hf : Function.Injective f) :
    Function.Injective ((Ideal.Quotient.mk (nilradical S)).comp f) :=
  (RingHom.injective_iff_ker_eq_bot _).2 <| eq_bot_iff.2 fun _ hr =>
    Ideal.mem_bot.mpr (isNilpotent_iff_eq_zero.mp ((IsNilpotent.map_iff hf).mp
      (mem_nilradical.mp (Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.mp hr))))

/-- Let `k` be a field of exponential characteristic `p`, `A` a reduced integrally closed ring
and `i : A →+* T` an injective map into a `k`-algebra such that every element of `T` has a
`p ^ n`-th power in the image of `i`. Write `S = T ⧸ nilradical T`. Then the map to `Spec T` from
the spectrum of the integral closure of `S` in its total ring of fractions is a universal
homeomorphism. -/
public theorem universalHomeomorphism_normalization_of_pow_mem_range
    {k A T : Type u} [Field k] [CommRing A] [CommRing T] [Algebra k T]
    [_root_.IsReduced A] [IsIntegrallyClosed A]
    (i : A →+* T) (hi : Function.Injective i) (p : ℕ) [ExpChar k p]
    (hp : ∀ t : T, ∃ n : ℕ, t ^ p ^ n ∈ i.range) :
    let S := T ⧸ nilradical T
    UniversalHomeomorphism (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom
      ((algebraMap S (integralClosure S (FractionRing S))).comp
        (Ideal.Quotient.mk (nilradical T))))) := by
  intro S
  have : _root_.IsReduced S :=
    (Ideal.isRadical_iff_quotient_reduced _).mp (Ideal.radical_isRadical _)
  let : Algebra A S := ((Ideal.Quotient.mk (nilradical T)).comp i).toAlgebra
  have hj : Function.Injective (algebraMap A S) := injective_quotient_nilradical_comp i hi
  have hp' : ∀ s : S, ∃ n : ℕ, s ^ p ^ n ∈ (algebraMap A S).range := by
    intro s
    obtain ⟨t, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective s
    obtain ⟨n, a, ha⟩ := hp t
    refine ⟨n, a, ?_⟩
    show (Ideal.Quotient.mk _) (i a) = _
    rw [ha, map_pow]
  have hpos := exists_pos_pow_mem_range_of_expChar (k := k) (algebraMap A S) p hp'
  have : Algebra.IsIntegral A S := isIntegral_of_pos_pow_mem_range hpos
  have hreg : A⁰ ≤ (S⁰).comap (algebraMap A S) :=
    nonZeroDivisors_le_comap_of_pow_mem_range (algebraMap A S) hj hpos
  let B := integralClosure S (FractionRing S)
  let f : T →+* B := (algebraMap S B).comp (Ideal.Quotient.mk (nilradical T))
  show UniversalHomeomorphism (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom f))
  have hinj : Function.Injective (algebraMap S B) := fun _ _ hab =>
    IsFractionRing.injective S (FractionRing S) (congrArg Subtype.val hab)
  apply universalHomeomorphism_specMap_of_pow_mem_range (k := k) f p
  · exact fun t ht => Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.mp
      (hinj (by simpa only [f, RingHom.comp_apply, map_zero] using RingHom.mem_ker.mp ht))
  · intro b
    obtain ⟨n, s, hs⟩ :=
      exists_pow_mem_range_normalization_of_isIntegrallyClosed hj hreg p hp' b
    obtain ⟨t, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective s
    exact ⟨n, t, hs⟩

/-- A separably generated extension of fields `K/k` is separable in the sense of
`Algebra.IsSeparableExtension`. -/
public theorem isSeparableExtension_of_isSeparablyGenerated
    (k K : Type*) [Field k] [Field K] [Algebra k K]
    [Algebra.IsSeparablyGenerated k K] : Algebra.IsSeparableExtension k K := by
  obtain ⟨s, hs, hsep⟩ :=
    Algebra.IsSeparablyGenerated.isSeparable (k := k) (K := K)
  constructor
  intro L _
  obtain ⟨t, ht, hsep⟩ :=
    exists_isTranscendenceBasis_and_isSeparable_of_isSeparable_adjoin_of_essFiniteType
      (L := L) hs hsep
  exact ⟨t, ht, hsep⟩

/-- Every extension of fields `K/k` factors as `k → F → K` with `F/k` separable, in the sense of
`Algebra.IsSeparableExtension`, and `K/F` purely inseparable. -/
public theorem exists_separable_purelyInseparable_factorization
    (k K : Type u) [Field k] [Field K] [Algebra k K] :
    ∃ (F : Type u) (_ : Field F) (_ : Algebra k F) (_ : Algebra F K),
      IsScalarTower k F K ∧ Algebra.IsSeparableExtension k F ∧ IsPurelyInseparable F K := by
  obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ := exists_isTranscendenceBasis k K
  let F₀ := IntermediateField.adjoin k s
  have : Algebra.IsAlgebraic F₀ K := by
    have h := hs.isAlgebraic_field
    rwa [show Set.range ((↑) : s → K) = s from Subtype.range_coe] at h
  let F := separableClosure F₀ K
  let : Algebra k F := ((algebraMap F₀ F).comp (algebraMap k F₀)).toAlgebra
  have : IsScalarTower k F₀ F := IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq' rfl
  have : IsScalarTower k F K := IsScalarTower.to₁₃₄ k F₀ F K
  let x : s → F := fun t => algebraMap F₀ F ⟨t.1, IntermediateField.subset_adjoin k s t.2⟩
  have hx : IsTranscendenceBasis k x :=
    .of_comp (IsScalarTower.toAlgHom k F K) (algebraMap F K).injective hs
  have hsep : Algebra.IsSeparable (IntermediateField.adjoin k (Set.range x)) F := by
    let H := IntermediateField.adjoin k (Set.range x)
    let j : F →ₐ[k] K := IsScalarTower.toAlgHom k F K
    have hmap : H.map j = F₀ := by
      rw [IntermediateField.adjoin_map, ← Set.range_comp]
      show IntermediateField.adjoin k (Set.range ((↑) : s → K)) = F₀
      rw [Subtype.range_coe]
    let e : H ≃ₐ[k] F₀ := (IntermediateField.equivMap H j).trans
      (IntermediateField.equivOfEq hmap)
    apply Algebra.IsSeparable.of_equiv_equiv e.symm.toRingEquiv (RingEquiv.refl F)
    ext r
    show j ((e.symm r : H) : F) = (r : K)
    simpa only [e, AlgEquiv.trans_apply, IntermediateField.equivOfEq_apply,
      IntermediateField.coe_equivMap_apply] using
      congrArg (fun t : F₀ => (t : K)) (e.apply_symm_apply r)
  have : Algebra.IsSeparablyGenerated k F := ⟨Set.range x, hx.to_subtype_range, hsep⟩
  exact ⟨F, inferInstance, inferInstance, inferInstance, inferInstance,
    isSeparableExtension_of_isSeparablyGenerated k F, inferInstance⟩

open scoped TensorProduct in
/-- **The normalization comparison after a field extension is a universal homeomorphism.** Let
`R` be a normal `k`-algebra and `K/k` an arbitrary extension of fields. Write `T = R ⊗[k] K` and
`S = T ⧸ nilradical T`. Then the map to `Spec T` from the spectrum of the integral closure of
`S` in its total ring of fractions is a universal homeomorphism. -/
public theorem universalHomeomorphism_normalization_tensorProduct_of_normal
    {k K R : Type u} [Field k] [Field K] [CommRing R]
    [Algebra k K] [Algebra k R] (hR : IsNormalRing R) :
    let T := R ⊗[k] K
    let S := T ⧸ nilradical T
    UniversalHomeomorphism (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom
      ((algebraMap S (integralClosure S (FractionRing S))).comp
        (Ideal.Quotient.mk (nilradical T))))) := by
  obtain ⟨F, _, _, _, _, _, _⟩ := exists_separable_purelyInseparable_factorization k K
  let A := F ⊗[k] R
  have : Algebra.IsGeometricallyNormal k F :=
    Algebra.IsGeometricallyNormal.of_isSeparableExtension
  have hA : IsNormalRing A :=
    Algebra.IsGeometricallyNormal.isNormalRing_tensorProduct_of_isNormalRing k F R hR
  have : _root_.IsReduced A := hA.isReduced
  have : IsIntegrallyClosed A := hA.isIntegrallyClosed
  let e : (A ⊗[F] K) ≃+* (R ⊗[k] K) :=
    (Algebra.TensorProduct.comm F A K).toRingEquiv.trans
      ((Algebra.TensorProduct.cancelBaseChange k F F K R).toRingEquiv.trans
        (Algebra.TensorProduct.comm k K R).toRingEquiv)
  let i : A →+* R ⊗[k] K := e.toRingHom.comp (algebraMap A (A ⊗[F] K))
  have hi : Function.Injective i := e.injective.comp
    (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeLeft_injective (S := A) (algebraMap F K).injective)
  have : ExpChar F (ringExpChar k) :=
    expChar_of_injective_ringHom (algebraMap k F).injective (ringExpChar k)
  apply universalHomeomorphism_normalization_of_pow_mem_range (k := k) i hi (ringExpChar k)
  intro t
  obtain ⟨n, a, ha⟩ :=
    IsPurelyInseparable.exists_pow_pow_mem_range_tensorProduct_of_expChar
      (ringExpChar k) (e.symm t)
  refine ⟨n, a, ?_⟩
  show e (algebraMap A (A ⊗[F] K) a) = t ^ (ringExpChar k) ^ n
  rw [ha, map_pow, e.apply_symm_apply]

end AlgebraicGeometry

end
